# TODO_progress_display
#
# Design: DAG progress visualization with "power flow" rendering.
#
# Replace verbose line-dump shell output with a live DAG visualization
# that shows nodes lighting up as execution progresses — think SimCity
# (2013) power grid flowing through infrastructure.
#
# Architecture: renderer-agnostic data model + pluggable display backends
# (terminal first, web later — same underlying state).

## Problem

Current shell output dumps sequential log lines:

    [parse_read_files]
      contents: {234 entries}
    [render_markdown]
      markdown: # Code Snapshot...
    [execute_gist]
      exit_code: 0
      stderr: - Creating gist snapshot.md
    [parse_gist_response]
      url: https://gist.github.com/...

This is functional but:
- No sense of overall progress or structure
- Can't see which nodes are waiting, running, or done
- No visual relationship between nodes (edges are invisible)
- Long pipelines produce walls of text that scroll off screen

## Design: Three-layer architecture

    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    │  Layer 3: Renderers (terminal, web, CI)             │
    │  - TerminalRenderer: ANSI TUI with live updates     │
    │  - WebRenderer: JSON/SSE stream for browser UI      │
    │  - CiRenderer: existing CI group/annotation output  │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │  Layer 2: DagProgress (renderer-agnostic state)     │
    │  - NodeState, EdgeState, timing, output summaries   │
    │  - Snapshot-based: renderers poll or subscribe       │
    ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    │  Layer 1: ProgressObserver (execution hook)         │
    │  - Plugs into execute_flat() loop                   │
    │  - Emits events: NodeStarted, NodeCompleted, etc.   │
    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

## Layer 1: ProgressObserver trait

Plugs into the existing execute_flat() loop in core/exec/src/execute.rs.
The current loop already processes nodes in topo order — we just need
callbacks at the right points.

```rust
/// Observer for DAG execution progress.
///
/// Called by the executor at key points during DAG execution.
/// Implementations control what happens with progress information:
/// terminal display, web streaming, logging, etc.
pub trait ProgressObserver: Send {
    /// Called once before execution begins with the full DAG topology.
    /// The observer uses this to build its internal layout/graph.
    fn on_dag_start(&mut self, snapshot: &DagSnapshot);

    /// Called when a node begins execution.
    fn on_node_start(&mut self, node_id: &NodeId);

    /// Called when a node completes successfully.
    /// `summary` contains a compact representation of outputs (not raw values).
    fn on_node_complete(&mut self, node_id: &NodeId, summary: OutputSummary);

    /// Called when a node fails.
    fn on_node_failed(&mut self, node_id: &NodeId, error: &str);

    /// Called when a node is skipped (guard predicate failed).
    fn on_node_skipped(&mut self, node_id: &NodeId);

    /// Called when a node is intercepted (dry-run mock).
    fn on_node_intercepted(&mut self, node_id: &NodeId, summary: OutputSummary);

    /// Called once after all nodes have been processed.
    fn on_dag_complete(&mut self, elapsed: Duration);
}
```

