## Layer 2: DagProgress state machine

Renderer-agnostic state that any display backend can consume.
This is the "model" — it knows nothing about terminals or HTML.

```rust
/// Live state of a DAG execution.
///
/// Built from ProgressObserver events. Renderers read this to know
/// what to display. Can be serialized to JSON for web transport.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]
pub struct DagProgress {
    pub nodes: HashMap<NodeId, NodeProgress>,
    pub edges: HashMap<(NodeId, NodeId), EdgeProgress>,
    pub topo_order: Vec<NodeId>,
    pub phase: DagPhase,
    pub elapsed: Duration,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]
pub enum DagPhase {
    NotStarted,
    Running { current_node: NodeId },
    Completed { elapsed: Duration },
    Failed { node: NodeId, error: String },
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]
pub struct NodeProgress {
    pub id: NodeId,
    pub label: String,
    pub state: NodeState,
    pub is_boundary: bool,
    pub summary: Option<OutputSummary>,
    pub elapsed: Option<Duration>,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize)]
pub enum NodeState {
    /// Not yet reached in topo order
    Pending,
    /// Currently executing
    Running,
    /// Finished successfully
    Completed,
    /// Finished with error
    Failed,
    /// Guard predicate skipped this node
    Skipped,
    /// Intercepted by dry-run mock
    Intercepted,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize)]
pub enum EdgeState {
    /// No data has flowed yet
    Idle,
    /// Source node completed — data is "flowing" to target
    /// (visual: animated pulse/highlight)
    Flowing,
    /// Target node consumed the data — edge is done
    Done,
    /// Source was skipped — edge will never carry data
    Dead,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]
pub struct EdgeProgress {
    pub from: NodeId,
    pub to: NodeId,
    pub state: EdgeState,
}
```

### State transitions (the "power flow")

The SimCity power-grid effect comes from edge state transitions:

    1. DAG starts:     all nodes=Pending, all edges=Idle
    2. Node A starts:  A=Running
    3. Node A done:    A=Completed, edges(A→*)=Flowing
    4. Node B starts:  B=Running, edges(*→B)=Done
    5. Node B done:    B=Completed, edges(B→*)=Flowing
    ...
    N. Last node done: DAG=Completed

The "Flowing" state is the key visual moment — it represents data
traveling along the edge. A renderer can show this as:
  - Terminal: brief color pulse on the edge character (─ → ═ → ─)
  - Web: CSS animation along the SVG path
  - CI: no visual effect (just log output)

